        "United States Copyright Office filing fees described throughout this Section are charged directly by the United States Copyright Office. These fees are entirely separate from, and in addition to, Attorney’s fees described below. They are not part of Attorney’s compensation and are paid directly to the federal government.",
        "Copyright Office Filing Fees, Explained: As of the date of this Agreement, the Copyright Office charges $45.00 to file a single application online for one work with one author and one claimant that is not a work made for hire, and $65.00 to file a standard application online for most other claims, including works with multiple authors or claimants. Paper filing, where permitted, carries a fee of $125.00. These figures are published by the Copyright Office, are subject to change without notice to Attorney, and will be confirmed to Client at the time of filing.",
        "(A) Copyright Registration Application",
        "Attorney will prepare and file an application for federal copyright registration of the Work with the United States Copyright Office, including preparation of the deposit copy, submission of the applicable Copyright Office filing fee on Client’s behalf, and a response to one round of Copyright Office correspondence, if issued. Attorney will complete and file the application within ten (10) business days of receipt of all materials necessary to complete the application.",
        "Client elects: {{answers.works_elected}}, plus the applicable Copyright Office filing fee per work described above.",
        "This engagement covers registration of a single Work under one application. If Client later elects to register additional works, each additional work requires a separate application and fee, unless the works qualify for registration together under one of the Copyright Office’s group registration options for unpublished works, eligible serials, or short online literary works. Attorney will advise Client whether a particular group of works qualifies.",
        "(B) Acknowledgement Regarding Other Intellectual Property Protections (Excluded from this Agreement)",
        "Copyright registration protects the original literary authorship fixed in the Work itself. It does not protect titles, names, slogans, or short phrases used in connection with the Work, which may instead be eligible for trademark protection, and it does not protect any invention or functional feature described or depicted in the Work, which may instead be eligible for patent protection. Trademark and patent matters are both specifically excluded from this engagement. Attorney assists clients with trademark matters as a separate engagement upon request but does not provide patent services of any kind. Clients who wish to pursue patent protection should consult separate patent counsel."
